  "protocol": "At centre 0 take complete three-tick port reads until informative (difference 4). Four nulls have probability 1/8 each and only translate. For a localized launch the bright/even and dark/odd informative outcomes have equal chances. Flip the sign of one tracked occupied clock cell on the even branch. Both now have the same odd dipole up to sign/translation. Route to centre 2; on each informative difference-1 probe, add +1 for bright and -1 for dark, retrying all nulls. At +m stop; at -m apply D|j>=(-1)^j|j> then stop. Route to each requested centre after previous probes by reading every single base hop; these act by a known translation and sign. All four null outcomes, verdict signs, and deadlines are counted. Coherences and orientation inside conjugate pairs are not claimed to be standardized.",
  "algebra": "Low k={1,7}; high={3,5}. In the odd sector an informative bright probability is (2+sqrt(2))/4 or its complement. The untouched sector is a sampling representation. Each stopped branch has the same residual high weight epsilon, and each verdict has marginal probability 1/2 in the symmetric initial odd ensemble. In JSON a,b encode a+b sqrt(2). A finite cap records the surviving mass jointly.",
